 the consolidated tip (the post-fix tree), not on each block's own pre-fix sha: every audit blocked on the tip it read and the fixes landed as the next commits, so the pre-fix witnesses are the audits' own executed evidence and the relay artifacts per block. The identity unit's cache-reuse admission and definition-hash fold are EXCISED by the contract's pre-committed stop rule (the same-crate ProbedOp construction oracle could not be made complete: a use-rename and a mutated-copy return stayed invisible); the typed PROBED_OPS table stays with cross-crate sealing proven by the compiler and NO same-crate property claimed, because nothing folds an admission row into a durable hash. #546 and #562 item 3 stay open with the blind spots recorded. The two syn call-site oracles (submit seam, raw deleters) record the target path in any expression position over every compiled non-test .rs file; their residual is a bypass that duplicates the seam's body, caught by the oracle and never by the type system. The placed-gang birth epoch is read before probe_claim and begin_release's flip-before-bump order is pinned by a park point; the claim loop's own epoch path is unchanged. GRAPH (#515) is excised by its pre-committed stop rule and stays open with four executed design rounds. The #551 mining byte pin is captured from this PR's first Linux CI run and committed as a follow-up on the same PR. The lead-gate library's own residual arms, each marked `# R12-RESIDUAL` and each a rejection or a bounded run rather than a proof \u2014 _pre_fix_anticipation_rejection, _r12_anticipation_rejection, _r12_attack_command_denied, _r12_is_inspector_only, _r12_mutations_array_rejection, _r12_validate_and_run_entry, _resolve_worktree_cwd, _run_attack_command, cmd_export_anticipation, cmd_export_attestation \u2014 stay residuals: an attack command is re-executed and hash-matched at check time in a clean worktree, never re-derived; an inspector-only command proves presence, not behaviour; the mutations array is a labeled sample capped at three, never an exhaustive sweep.", "ts": "2026-09-17T13:15:01.474396+00:00", "unit_branch": "feat/500-wave5"}
